{
  "an9.12:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 9.12 ",
  "an9.12:0.2": "2. The Lion’s Roar ",
  "an9.12:0.3": "With Residue ",
  "an9.12:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "an9.12:1.2": "Then Venerable Sāriputta robed up in the morning and, taking his bowl and robe, entered Sāvatthī for alms. ",
  "an9.12:1.3": "Then it occurred to him, ",
  "an9.12:1.4": "“It’s too early to wander for alms in Sāvatthī. ",
  "an9.12:1.5": "Why don’t I visit the monastery for the wanderers of other religions?” ",
  "an9.12:1.6": "Then he went to the monastery for the wanderers of other religions and exchanged greetings with the wanderers there. ",
  "an9.12:1.7": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side. ",
  "an9.12:2.1": "Now at that time while those wanderers of other religions were sitting together this discussion came up among them: ",
  "an9.12:2.2": "“Reverends, no one who dies with residue is exempt from hell, the animal realm, or the ghost realm. They’re not exempt from places of loss, bad places, the underworld.” ",
  "an9.12:2.3": "Sāriputta neither approved nor rejected that statement of the wanderers of other religions. ",
  "an9.12:2.4": "He rose from his seat, thinking, ",
  "an9.12:2.5": "“I will learn the meaning of this statement from the Buddha himself.” ",
  "an9.12:2.6": "Then Sāriputta wandered for alms in Sāvatthī. After the meal, on his return from almsround, he went 